    rdf:value "- Additional information from staff reads, \"The handwritten text of the Journal in German was transliterated and reviewed by Ernst Herzfeld's former collaborator, Friedrich Krefter, with the assistance of his wife, Maria Krefter. Please contact the Archives for digital access to the transliterated copy.\"" .

kg:note_ref6367_scopecontent_0_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "From Berlin to Pasargadae via Basra, Baghdad, Paikuli, Tāq-i Bustān, Hamadan, Teheran, Khurha, Qum and Isfahan." .

kg:note_ref6367_scopecontent_1_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "- FSA A.6 01.04, on which Joseph Upton's classification mentions \"N-83\", provides an account of an expedition (February 14, 1923 to November 14, 1923) from Berlin (Germany) to Pasargadae (Iran), via Bombay (india) and Karrachi (Pakistan), then following ancient caravan roads via Baghdad (Iraq), Paikuli (Iraq), hamadan (Iran), Tehran (Iran), Isfahan (Iran), to finally reach Shiraz (Iran) and the monuments in its vicinity." .

