kg:note_ref6667_arrangement_0_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "In the original arrangement of the Ernst Herzfeld Archive, Travel Journals were included in a larger body of diverse material acknowledged by Ernst Herzfeld as his study collection. In the early 1970s, Joseph Upton, for research purpose, rearranged the collection and created a specific series (Ernst Herzfeld Papers, Series 1: Travel Journals, 1905-1928) for eight travel journals. For some reason, Upton has given this journal an accession number related to the series he created for the notebooks (Ernst Herzfeld Papers, Series 3: Notebooks, 1904-1946, 1957, n.d.), probably following Herzfeld's original organization." .

kg:note_ref6667_odd_0_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "Ernst Herzfeld Papers, N-85" .

kg:note_ref6667_odd_0_p_1 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "FSA A.6 03.085" .

kg:note_ref6667_odd_0_p_2 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "FSA A.6 01.06" .

kg:note_ref6667_odd_1_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "- Additional information from staff reads, \"Only part of the handwritten text of the Journal in German was transliterated and reviewed by Ernst Herzfeld's former collaborator, Friedrich Krefter, with the assistance of his wife, Maria Krefter. Please contact the Archives for digital access to the transliterated copy.\"" .

kg:note_ref6667_scopecontent_0_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "The Journal ends at Salami, just before Herzfeld reached Mashhad. From Bombay to Mashhad via Kabul, Sistan (Kūh-i Khwāja and Shahristān), Kuhistan (Birjand, Khargird). Journal No.II which would cover the stay in Mashhad and the trip to Tehran via Sangbast, Nishapur, Sabzevar, Damghan, Bistam, Radkan and Simnan is not in the Archive." .

kg:note_ref6667_scopecontent_1_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "- FSA A.6 01.06, on which Joseph Upton's classification mentions \"N-85\", provides an account of Herzfeld's visits (December 1924 and January 1925) to museums in Bombay and Delhi (India), Kabul (Afghanistan), Karrachi and Peshawar (Pakistan), as well as an account of an expedition (January 25, 1925 to March 21, 1925) from Zahedan, in the province of Sistan and Baluchestan (Iran), to Salami (Iran), a village south of Mashhad (Iran) in the province of Khorasan. During this trip which ultimately led him to Tehran (Iran), Herzfeld visited Kuh-i Khwaja (Iran), Shahristan (Iran), Birjand (Iran), Qa'In (Iran), and Khargird (Iran). Finally, many historical notes are to be found throughout the diary." .

kg:note_ref6667_scopecontent_1_p_1 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "- Original handwritten title on cover reads: \"Ernst Herzfeld; Afghanistan - Ostpersien I, 1924-1925\"" .

kg:note_ref6667_scopecontent_1_p_10 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
